  "source_review": [
    "Both formats execute complete native draw and conversion encoders, compare every active pixel including alpha through surface_gpu::compare, and publish PASS only after specific submission completion, successful mapping/full equality and all three error scopes. References are never uploaded to the encoders.",
    "Each cancellation guard poisons the outer owned lease, discards its encoder, performs exactly one empty flush, polls that submission, rejects output/compatibility/reusable access, pops all three scopes, and publishes PASS only on success.",
    "All six reachable cancellation callback cutpoints are exercised: initial guard, clear/rectangle/image/glyph guards, and conversion guard. Cancellation allocations are separate from the 13 allocation counters in each successful-frame sequence.",
    "Frame sequence changes source images, glyph coverage/row origins, clear colors and uniforms without size changes, then no-input and clear-only layouts, hidden work, width/height/format, and a fresh context over the same Device/Queue. Old buffers are destroyed before incompatible replacement allocation.",
    "Frame counts are harness-local allocation/checkout/eviction counters; 13 frame evictions include the final cached set. All three adapters have the same exact plan storage amounts independently recalculated from packed/padded pixels, draw uniforms, conversion uniform and input arena.",
    "The new reuse validator requires exact inventory prefix, ordered six cancellation rows, ordered 28 frame routes and cache decisions, dimension/comparison lengths, bounded planned/readback bytes and exact terminal totals. It uses bounds rather than exact per-fixture planned values; this audit additionally checks exact values.",
    "run_surface_host defaults remain validate_run and empty extra_helpers. Its previous source equals current source after exactly the three additive seam substitutions; old CLI authorization/signals, validation, binary/loader/helper pre/post checks, fresh output and stop-on-first-failure behavior remain unchanged.",
    "run_reuse_host explicitly supplies its validator and includes itself in pre/post helper bindings. Host success follows every supervised positive exit, complete cleanup, empty checker/supervisor stderr and final identity recheck."
  ],
